--- kps-S31ah findings ---
TOOLKIT VALIDATED: the generator mechanically rediscovers THM-200 (H=7 gap), THM-115 (H=21 gap),
THM-029 (alpha1=3 forbidden n<=6), THM-201 (K3 not realizable as Omega), THM-202 (P4 not realizable).
=> the abstract engine reproduces the hand-proved certificates, confirming it as a technique generator.

KEY REFRAMING: K_m realizable as Omega(T) <=> 1+2m achievable as a SINGLE-COMPONENT H <=> m not in {3,10}.
(I(K_m,2)=1+2m since a clique's only independent sets are singletons+empty.) So:
  H=7 gap  = K_3 not realizable as Omega (THM-201)
  H=21 gap = K_10 not realizable as Omega (the hard THM-115 single-component case)
The Omega-realizability spectrum is SPARSE (1/34 graphs on 5 vertices); realized small-Omega are
clique-like (cycles pairwise-share around common vertices). Forbidden = "spread" graphs (paths, anticliques).
